-- ============================================================================
-- DR6 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Casing & Tubing Design, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: the tubing string, which is a casing string that is
-- ALLOWED TO MOVE. It is not cemented, so it can change length, load its
-- packer and buckle, and a cemented string can do none of those. Only three
-- things change over the life of a completion, and every force here is a
-- CHANGE in one of them from the packer setting condition. The Lubinski and
-- Hammerlindl planning forms give piston, ballooning and thermal; three length
-- terms; a stroke verdict; and the Dawson-Paslay buckling limits.
--
-- THE FINDING, AND m05 IS BUILT ON IT. The three published operating cases
-- each hit a DIFFERENT limit. Production heating buckles HELICALLY and is
-- comfortably inside its stroke, and it has the BEST packer safety factor of
-- the three at 5.416989018921467. Injection cooling does not buckle at all and
-- strokes out. Stimulation has the WORST packer safety factor at
-- 1.448941812184961 and does not buckle either. There is no design case,
-- because buckling responds to the SIGN of the force through a maximum against
-- zero while the packer and stroke checks respond to its MAGNITUDE, and only
-- one of the three cases is in compression. That is the same shape as the
-- Professional tier's result, where a case named after burst was governed by
-- the triaxial check.
--
-- TWO EXACT RESULTS THE TIER TURNS ON. The helical buckling limit is
-- 1.8284271247461903 times the sinusoidal one, which is two root two less one,
-- on every string in every hole at every inclination, because both limits are
-- the same square root times a different pure constant. And the STROKE WINDOW
-- is exactly twice the stroke over the expansion coefficient times the length,
-- which is 100 degrees on this completion, whatever the pressures do: the
-- total length is a straight line in temperature whose slope contains no
-- pressure, so the pressures slide the window and never widen it. The engine's
-- bisected edges at minus 34.82534863819683 and 65.17465136180317 agree with
-- the closed form to a part in ten million.
--
-- A THIRD RESULT, IN m04. Neither the thermal FORCE nor either buckling limit
-- contains a length. A 500 m string and a 5000 m string give the same thermal
-- force for the same mean temperature change, and the same buckling limits in
-- the same hole. The thermal LENGTH change does contain the length, and
-- holding that pair together is the point of the module.
--
-- WHAT THIS TIER TEACHES AND CERTIFIES NOWHERE: the buckling length term, the
-- annular pressure buildup coupling, seal and buckled-string friction, the
-- erosional velocity limit as a design criterion, connection sealing, casing
-- wear and fatigue. 20260830_dr6_casingtubing_go_live.sql asserts it.
--
-- Numeric sweep and tier-leakage sweep as for the tiers below: 0 unresolved
-- literals, 0 downward leaks, 0 same-tier answer prints.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

